if you've been itching for another dose  of trials since the release of evolution  in 2012 there's not much longer to wait  for the next gen ready trials fusion  aside from being the first in the series  to hit the PlayStation platform the  PlayStation 4 is also the first to  feature stunts you can perform actual  proper tricks on your bike simply by  wiggling the right analog stick the  tricks themselves are based on freestyle  motocross and are hooked into the  physics system so when you're hanging  off the back of your bike performing a  superman the extra weight means you've  got to quickly adjust your angle so you  don't spin out the tricks look awesome  in action and there are specific levels  designed just for them featuring big  jumps and ramps as well as fmx specific  challenges speaking of challenges there  are over 120 in the game including some  unique ones that have you flying a  rocket powered bike through the air and  playing tennis with the disgruntled  penguin the meat of the game still  involved guiding your motocross bike  over ever more challenging obstacles  though and it's enormously fun as ever  to play levels especially bright and  colorful this time around gone are the  overly brown areas of old replaced  instead with sharp shiny surfaces and  heaps of bright colors the levels are  even zanier too with all sorts of  explosions and moving platforms that try  and send you crashing headfirst into a  wall should two wheels not be enough for  you fusion also features a quad bike  there are some levels specifically  designed for the increased speeds and  slightly more forgiving handling of the  quad but you can take it out on any  track including the multiplayer ones  which makes for some wonderfully  topsy-turvy races trials fusion is  shaping up to be just as compulsive and  experienced as its predecessors and it  looks mighty fine to boot it's also  coming to retail with retail versions  coming bundled with a season pass that  gives you access to future DLC  expansions and content look out for it  on pc playstation 4 xbox one and xbox  360 soon  you
 

